---
import Figure from "../Figure.astro";
---
<Figure width="wide">
  <Fragment slot="controls">
    <div class="seg" id="cxm"><button data-m="cost" class="on">Dollars</button><button data-m="calls">Model calls</button><button data-m="gpus">GPUs</button><button data-m="size">Model size</button></div>
  </Fragment>
  <div class="chart" id="cost"></div>
  <div class="legend" id="costleg"></div>
  <p class="scroll-hint">Swipe sideways to see the whole chart.</p>
  <Fragment slot="caption">
    <b>Figure 6.</b> One run of a recursive self-improvement system, as each paper reports it on its own task. The
    tasks differ, so the rows show scale, not a ranking. <b>Dollars</b> are model spend at API list prices, as the other
    papers report theirs; SCiEL's own model runs on two H100s shared by parallel runs, whose rental for a whole run
    would be roughly $25 to $90 (6 to 15 hours at $2 to $3 per GPU-hour). The yellow marks compare with SCiEL's costliest
    run and are left out where a figure is not the cost of one run: the Huxley–Gödel Machine reports $5,000 for all its
    experiments together, and Dream-RSI's figure is its own estimate for one search on its costliest task.
    <b>Model size</b> counts total parameters; gpt-oss-120b and Qwen3-Coder-480B are mixtures of experts with 5.1B and
    35B active. Sources: Red Queen Gödel Machine (<a class="cite" href="#ref-23">Iacob et al., 2026</a>), whose authors
    also price Hyperagents' search tokens (<a class="cite" href="#ref-10">Zhang et al., 2026</a>); TTT-Discover
    (<a class="cite" href="#ref-4">Yuksekgonul et al., 2026</a>); ThetaEvolve (<a class="cite" href="#ref-12">Wang et al., 2025b</a>);
    MASS (<a class="cite" href="#ref-5">Lee et al., 2026</a>); Huxley–Gödel Machine (<a class="cite" href="#ref-9">Wang et al., 2025a</a>);
    SICA (<a class="cite" href="#ref-8">Robeyns et al., 2025</a>); Darwin Gödel Machine (<a class="cite" href="#ref-7">Zhang et al., 2025</a>);
    Dream-RSI (<a class="cite" href="#ref-24">Zheng et al., 2026</a>).
  </Fragment>
</Figure>
